]},{"k":"26083d95aec7","n":16,"p":[[0,1,"And"],[0,5,"to those <i>tanna’im</i> who expound this"],[5,16,"“The owner of the ox shall be clear,” to … half … indemnity … payment … for … offspring … from where do they … benefiting from … hide?","<b>“The owner of the ox shall be clear,” to</b> teach that the owner of an innocuous ox, i.e., one that is not known to cause damage with the intent to injure, is exempt from the payment of <b>half</b> of the <b>indemnity</b> incurred if that ox killed a person, or that he is exempt from <b>payment</b> of damages <b>for</b> miscarried <b>offspring</b> if his ox gores a pregnant woman and causes her to miscarry; <b>from where do they</b> derive this prohibition against <b>benefiting from</b> the ox’s <b>hide?</b>"]],"w":{"0":"And … to those","1":"tanna’im","2":"who expound","4":"this","5":"The owner of","6":"the ox shall","7":"be clear","8":"to … half","10":"indemnity … payment … for … from where do","11":"offspring … they","12":"benefiting from","13":"hide"},"g":[[0,2,"ולאותם תנאים","a"],[2,5,"שמוציאים אותו את הביטוי הזה","a"],[14,16,"מניין להם","a"]]},{"k":"1f8d84634b1b","n":6,"p":[[0,1,"from"],[1,2,"“Its flesh"],[3,5,"et besaro … that which is secondary to the flesh,","<b>et besaro</b></i><b>].”</b> The verse could have been formulated: <i>Velo ye’akhel besaro</i>, which already means: And its flesh shall not be eaten. The addition of the word “<i>et</i>” teaches that the prohibition applies also to <b>that which is secondary to the flesh,</b>"],[5,6,"And the other"]],"w":{"0":"from","1":"Its flesh","3":"et besaro … which is secondary to the","4":"that … flesh","5":"And the other"},"g":[[5,6,"והאחר","a"]]}]}
